<title>THAILAND: Thai stock market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Thai stock market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Stock Exchange of Thailand (SET) was closed on Tuesday for the Constitution Day holiday.</p>
<p>On Monday, the SET Index gained 12.57 points, or 1.43 percent increase, to close at 889.46 on 2.7 billion baht ($108 million) turnover. The SET-50 index rose 1.35 points to 67.49.</p>
<p>The market will reopen on Tuesday.</p>
<p>($1 = 25 baht)</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
